{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0191uYsR3xz2g6BktpchQjWQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have enough context about AAAI. Based on the AAAI-26 statistics, the acceptance rate is 17.6%. Let me use the standard AAAI review scale which is typically 1-10:\n\n- 10: Award quality\n- 9: Strong accept\n- 8: Accept\n- 7: Weak accept\n- 6: Borderline accept\n- 5: Borderline reject  \n- 4: Weak reject\n- 3: Reject\n- 2: Strong reject\n- 1: Trivial or wrong\n\n\nAAAI also evaluates papers across significance, novelty, soundness, clarity, reproducibility, related work coverage, and reviewer confidence. Now I'll set up two parallel reviewers—one focusing on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and related work—and structure the review through independent assessments, cross-sharing, convergence, and a final consolidated report.\n\nLet me prepare detailed prompts for each reviewer with the key paper details: the vocabulary impoverishment finding as a shallow but generator-specific signal, the confirmed convergence hypothesis, and the critical experiments around feature ablation and cross-generator generalization.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3263,"cache_read_input_tokens":67207,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3263},"output_tokens":12,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad9f5738-9994-4640-8a26-12b004b49048","uuid":"533c01fb-1363-43ca-9529-c2bf45a59ab2"}
